ponsiveness in the critically ill</article-title><source>Crit Care Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>1402</fpage><lpage>1407</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16540963</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/01.CCM.0000215453.11735.06</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Solus-Biguenet</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Fleyfel</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Tavernier</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Kipnis</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Onimus</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Robin</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Lebuffe</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Decoene</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Pruvot</surname><given-names>FR</given-names></name><name><surname>Vallet</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Non-invasive prediction of fluid responsiveness during major hepatic surgery</article-title><source>Br J Anaesth</source><year>2006</year><volume>97</volume><fpage>808</fpage><lpage>816</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16980709</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/bja/ael250</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Natalini</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosano</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Taranto</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Faggian</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Vittorielli</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Bernardini</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Arterial versus plethysmographic dynamic indices to test responsiveness for testing fluid